<Project>
  <!--
    Repo-wide MSBuild defaults. Imported automatically by every project
    under this directory before the project's own .fsproj is evaluated.

    NU1510 suppression removed 2026-05-08 in Phase 11.C.1 (Paket -> CPM
    migration). Pre-migration, Paket emitted every transitive package as
    an explicit PackageReference in obj/*.paket.props, which triggered
    NU1510 against framework-provided packages. Post-migration, only
    direct PackageReference items remain (versions centralised in
    Directory.Packages.props), so NU1510 is now a meaningful signal —
    if it ever fires, it points at an explicit reference that should be
    pruned, not noise from generated files.
  -->

  <!--
    Phase 11.C.2 (2026-05-08) — common NuGet pack metadata. SDK companion
    fsprojs inherit these defaults; per-package overrides (PackageId,
    Description, etc.) live in each fsproj's <PropertyGroup>. Non-public-
    surface projects (App composition roots, modules, test harnesses,
    test packs, commercial-internal) opt out with <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    in their own fsproj.

    Initial version 0.1.0 across the board. SemVer-on-0.x policy: minor
    bumps may include breaking changes during 0.x; patch bumps remain
    non-breaking. Per-package <Version> overrides where a package needs
    to advance independently.
  -->
  <!--
    Phase 624 (2026-07-31) — FS0025 (incomplete pattern match) is an
    ERROR, not a hint.

    WHY. FS0025 is non-fatal and names only ONE example of the unmatched
    case. Measured directly against the F# 10 compiler: a match over a
    six-case DU missing THREE cases reports exactly one of them. So a
    warning that reports one instance of an N-instance problem produces
    an N-instance backlog, and the backlog is invisible because the build
    is green. That is not theoretical here — one hygiene bundle found a
    label function missing two arms where the warning had recorded one,
    and an audit-event table that had fallen 51 of 132 cases behind.

    Promoting it to an error does not make the message list every missing
    case — it still names one — but it forces the fix loop to CONTINUE
    until the match is exhaustive, instead of letting it stop after the
    single arm the warning happened to name.

    SCOPE. Tree-wide: every project that inherits this file. That is all
    161 projects in ToolUp.Forge.sln, plus Build.fsproj, tools/*,
    probes/*, dev/*, samples/*, and the templates/ projects that have no
    Directory.Build.props of their own.

    NOT COVERED, deliberately, and named here so the policy is not read
    as stronger than it is:
      • docs-snippets/ — documentation snippets are prose that must
        RESOLVE, not production code that must be lint-clean. It sits
        outside the solution, its sources are generated + gitignored, and
        it already turns all warnings off (Phase 620).
      • templates/safer/ and templates/platformsdk-solution/ — template
        CONTENT shipped to consumers via `dotnet new`. Each carries its
        own Directory.Build.props that does not import a parent, so
        MSBuild's walk stops there and this file never applies.
    Both exemptions are mirrored in `ArchitectureFitness.fs0025ExemptPrefixes`.

    THE WILDCARD HAZARD. Making this an error creates pressure to write
    `| _ ->` to get green. Do not. Measured: a wildcard emits no
    diagnostic at all, so it silences the check permanently and lets the
    table drift again invisibly — which is exactly how the 51-case gap
    opened. Enumerate the missing arms instead; if a case is genuinely
    unreachable, match it explicitly and fail loudly in its body.

    The two BROADER escape hatches — `#nowarn "25"` (whole file) and
    FS0025 in a project's NoWarn / WarningsNotAsErrors (whole project) —
    are pinned at zero by the Phase 624 tests in
    src/ToolUp.Platform.Tests/InProcess/ArchitectureFitnessTests.fs,
    which also assert this property is still here.

    Where a table over a closed DU must PROVABLY stay in step, the
    wildcard-immune mechanism is a reflection census over
    FSharpType.GetUnionCases — see AuditEventRegistryTests (Phase 114).
    It never reads the match expression, so no wildcard can fool it.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);FS0025</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Authors>Andrew J. Willshire</Authors>
    <Company>ToolUp Analytics Ltd (UK)</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) Andrew J. Willshire / ToolUp Analytics Ltd (UK)</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/ToolUp-Forge/toolup-forge</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/ToolUp-Forge/toolup-forge</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageTags>fsharp;full-stack;giraffe;fable;elmish;feliz</PackageTags>
    <Version>0.15.0</Version>
    <!--
      IsPackable defaults to true for SDK-style projects that produce a
      DLL. Non-publishable projects (App composition roots, modules,
      test packs, commercial-internal) opt out per-fsproj.
    -->
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <!--
      Phase 11.C.2 closure (2026-05-11) — packed-README default. Every
      packable SDK fsproj inherits <PackageReadmeFile>. Single-side
      companions where README.md is a sibling of the fsproj are auto-
      included via the <ItemGroup> below; cross-tier companions add
      an explicit per-fsproj <None Include="..\ToolUp.X\README.md"...>
      so all tiers share one parent README.
    -->
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!--
      Shared brand icon — single source of truth at repo-root icon.png.
      128x128 transparent PNG (NuGet's recommended display size). The
      packed <None Include> in the ItemGroup below ships the byte
      payload into every IsPackable nupkg; this property references it
      by filename so re-cutting the icon is one-file churn, not 48.
    -->
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Auto-include a sibling README.md for packable projects that have
    one. Cross-tier companions (where README.md lives in the parent
    docs directory, not next to the fsproj) add their own explicit
    <None Include="..\X\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' != 'false' And Exists('$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)\README.md')">
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Pack the shared brand icon into every IsPackable nupkg. <PackageIcon>
    in the PropertyGroup above references it by filename; this ItemGroup
    ships the byte payload from the single repo-root icon.png.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' != 'false'">
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
